  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Sinigrin potassium and U-87 MG cells, mediated through multiple intermediate targets. Sinigrin potassium is identified as a target of two distinct compounds, C-4-II and Npc167932, both of which are themselves targets of Thalifendine. Thalifendine, in turn, is known to have a target of U-87 MG cells, indicating a possible pathway through which Sinigrin potassium may influence cell behavior. Additionally, Sinigrin potassium is also linked to another target, Disintegrin and metalloproteinase domain-containing protein 28, which is also targeted by Thalifendine, further reinforcing the chain of interaction. The scores from the three paths suggest a consistent pattern of interaction, with varying levels of confidence in the strength of the relationships. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Sinigrin potassium and U-87 MG, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
